Package: NetSimR
Type: Package
Title: Non-Life Actuarial Pricing, Reserving, Reinsurance and Capital
Version: 0.4.0
Authors@R: c(person("Yiannis", "Parizas", email = "yiannis.parizas@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
                    comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0000-0523-0751")),
             person("The Inter Project Authors", role = "cph",
                    comment = "The Inter font, in inst/fonts"),
             person("The JetBrains Mono Project Authors", role = "cph",
                    comment = "The JetBrains Mono font, in inst/fonts"))
Description: Actuarial methods for pricing, reserving, reinsurance and
    capital in non-life insurance, with six 'shiny' tools that run them
    without writing code, and that also run in a web browser, without
    installing R, on the package's website.
    Pricing: a Tweedie family for generalised linear models of the loss
    cost, rate reviews with on-level premiums, the indicated rate change
    and Buhlmann-Straub credibility, and the simulation of claims from
    frequency and severity distributions with Pareto tails.
    Reserving: the chain ladder with Mack's standard errors and tail
    factors, the Bornhuetter-Ferguson, Benktander and Cape Cod methods, a
    bootstrap of the reserves, the one-year view of Merz and Wuthrich, the
    Munich chain ladder of paid and incurred claims, the growth curves of
    Clark (2003), a chain ladder for claims inflation, and actual against
    expected development.
    'IFRS' 17 and 'Solvency II': the discounting of reserves, the risk
    adjustment, and the standard formula's non-life premium and reserve
    risk.
    Reinsurance: excess of loss pricing with the burning cost, a Pareto
    model of the large losses and exposure rating with the MBBEFD curves
    of Bernegger (1997) <doi:10.2143/AST.27.1.563208> or a claim size
    distribution, the technical premium with reinstatements, and the
    comparison of reinsurance programmes by their cost and the capital
    they save.
    Capital: portfolios of several lines joined by a Gaussian or t copula,
    with value at risk, tail value at risk and capital allocation.
    Severity: capped means, exposure curves and increased limit factors
    for LogNormal, Gamma, Pareto, sliced LogNormal-Pareto and sliced
    Gamma-Pareto distributions, the density, distribution and quantile
    functions of the sliced distributions, and pure incurred but not
    reported (IBNR) exposure from a LogNormal or Gamma reporting delay.
    The tools are a claims simulator with reinsurance structures, and
    tools for fitting claim frequency and severity distributions, fitting
    generalised linear models with rate tables, claims reserving,
    reinsurance pricing and portfolio capital; each writes a report.
    Methods used in the package refer to
    Free for All by Yiannis Parizas (2023) <https://www.theactuary.com/2023/03/02/free-all>;
    Escaping the triangle by Yiannis Parizas (2019) <https://www.theactuary.com/features/2019/06/2019/06/05/escaping-triangle>;
    Taken to excess by Yiannis Parizas (2019) <https://www.theactuary.com/features/2019/03/2019/03/06/taken-excess>.
